  "description": "A shared-nothing io_uring runtime for .NET: one ring per reactor thread, inline completions, no system dependencies. The engine - reactor, connection, and the IRingHost client seam. Includes TLS termination on a bundled BoringSSL (libioxide_boringssl.so): the handshake driven over the ring, then optional kernel TLS (kTLS) offload, so handlers keep writing plaintext. kTLS needs the Linux tls module; nothing else does, and neither is loaded unless you use it.",
